    Bug 2047100 - Make the about dialog layout resize properly. r=vineet

    This is a problem only on Linux as dialogs can be resized even if they shouldn't.
    Some small CSS tweaks to let the content resize with the dialog if needed.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316907

diff --git a/mail/base/content/aboutDialog.css b/mail/base/content/aboutDialog.css
index efac4abad26..9bd6edfdf55 100644
--- a/mail/base/content/aboutDialog.css
+++ b/mail/base/content/aboutDialog.css
@@ -22,6 +22,14 @@
   }
 }

+html,
+body {
+  inline-size: 670px;
+  block-size: 400px;
+  min-inline-size: 670px;
+  min-block-size: 400px;
+}
+
 body {
   margin: 0;
   overflow: hidden;
@@ -35,18 +43,34 @@ body {
 }

 #aboutDialogContainer {
-  inline-size: 670px;
+  display: flex;
+  flex-direction: column;
+  inline-size: 100vw;
+  block-size: 100vh;
   color: var(--dialog-box-color);
   background-color: var(--dialog-background);
 }

+#clientBox {
+  display: grid;
+  grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
+  gap: 3px;
+  flex: 1 1 0;
+  background-color: var(--client-box-background);
+}
+
+#leftBox {
+  background-position: top center;
+  background-repeat: no-repeat;
+}
+
 #rightBox {
   background-image: url("chrome://branding/content/about-wordmark.svg");
   background-repeat: no-repeat;
   /* padding-top creates room for the wordmark */
   padding-block-start: 38px;
   margin-block-start: 20px;
-  margin-inline: 30px;
+  margin-inline-end: 30px;
   -moz-context-properties: fill;
   fill: currentColor;

